<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0">
  <head>
    <title>Home</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <outline text="Archestra operates in an extremely crowded environment."/>
    <outline text="There seems to be demand for something like Archestra, but it’s concentrated in enterprises that are putting agents into production, especially where agents touch sensitive data and can perform real actions."/>
    <outline text="Companies want to figure out how to secure agents, govern what they can do, track costs and performance, and plug them cleanly into existing infra."/>
    <outline text="Most visible “AI agent” products today (Lindy, Copilot, Glean, Dust, etc.) live at the application layer, giving knowledge workers assistants but not really solving infra‑level governance. "/>
    <outline text="Others like OpenClaw/Hermes can be a part of the homegrown solutions, but not focused on deterministic security, team collaboration or centralized MCP/compute governance."/>
    <outline text="Certain companies, like Every or Lindy, are experimenting with team-centered solutions, but their positioning is mostly about regular agentic features."/>
    <outline text="Archestra should own the space for responsible team-wide deployment and management of AI agents. "/>
    <outline text="How?" _strata_formatting="[{&quot;length&quot;:4,&quot;kind&quot;:&quot;bold&quot;,&quot;location&quot;:0}]">
      <outline text="State of AI Agent Data Leaks in the Enterprise ￼">
        <outline text="We produce a research report quantifying real‑world prompt injection / data‑exfiltration risks in enterprises (e.g., shadow agents, misconfigured copilots, leaked internal docs), using anonymized customer data, honeypots, and red‑team exercises."/>
        <outline text="Target outlets: Wired, MIT Technology Review"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Feature: AI Cost Bloodbath">
        <outline text="Aggregate notes from your clients and contacts to figure out the growth in inference pricing in the past 6 months to stress the importance of governance tools like Archestra"/>
        <outline text="Targets outlets: TechCrunch, VentureBeat, Business Insider"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Opinion: How to Build Secure AI for Enterprises">
        <outline text="Explain what are the main barriers for AI adoption in enterprise. Even AI-forward companies like Nvidia don&apos;t allow employees to connect chatbots to internal systems like Gmail or Slack. The company that do adopt it struggle with company-wide improvements as few people can master LLMs and build skills and connections for them. Without pushing this directly, we build the thesis for Achestra as the only solution. "/>
        <outline text="Target outlets: HBR, Business Insider"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Fire Drill: Is your agent secure?">
        <outline text="Build a publicly available website that can be fed as context to an agent in an attempt to crack it and make disclose information it shouldn&apos;t. Launch publicly on social media, use the attention to pitch tech media outlets."/>
        <outline text="Target outlets: VentureBeat, The Register, ZDNet"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
